  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Livelihoods for vulnerable HH in St Albert&apos;s - A fishery and poultry pilot project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project St Alberts would like to support  clients who are no longer bed bound with Livelihood interventions to enable them attain self-sustainability and restore their dignity in society. Two livelihoods projects will be initiated with support groups of people living with HIV. These projects will be light in terms of labour requirements ensuring that people living with HIV are capable of managing them. The aim is to improve their diet as well as reduce their presentation of opportunistic infections at the hospital OI Clinic. The proposed livelihood activities are fish farming and Quill/ indigenous chickens farming depending on support group preference. The project will target a total of 4 support groups selected by St Alberts based on need.</narrative>
  </description>
